001100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
001200 PROGRAM-ID.          TSTRMJOB.
001300 AUTHOR.              C HILLES.
001400 DATE-WRITTEN.        12/4/84.
001500 DATE-COMPILED.
002000*    THIS SUBPROGRAM IS DESGINED TO BE CALLED FROM AN OPTION
002100*    PROGRAM, OR FRONT END PROGRAM, TO A JOB STREAM.  THE
002200*    FRONT END PROGRAM DETERMINES USER OPTIONS FOR A BATCH
002300*    REPORT INTERACTIVELY (PROBABLY USING A VIEW SCREEN).
002400*    IT THEN PASSES THESE OPTIONS TO THIS SUBPROGRAM, ALONG
002500*    WITH OTHER PARAMETERS TELLING THIS SUBPROGRAM WHAT OBJECT
002600*    FILE TO RUN, ANY LIBRARYS TO USE, ETC.  THIS SUBPROGRAM
002700*    THEN CREATES A TEMPORARY FILE WHICH IS A JOB STREAM CONTAINING
002800*    ALL THE NEEDED JOB CARDS, RUN CARDS, ETC.  FOR THE JOB CARD
002900*    PASSWORD AND SIGNON, AND FOR REDEFINING PRINT FILE STATEMENTS,
003000*    IT READS FILES THAT MUST EXIST IN THE DB GROUP OF THE CME
003100*    ACCOUNT.  CIH.
003200
003300*   PARAMETERS
003400*   ----------
003500*
003600*    ALL THE FOLLOWING PARAMETERS ARE ACTUALLY PARTS OF A SINGLE
003700*    "COMMUNICATION AREA" PARAMETER PASSED TO THIS SUBPROGRAM:
003800*
003900*   STRM-RET-CODE   -  X(2)  -  A "00" IS RETURNED IF SUCCESSFUL
004000*                    EXECUTION.  THE COMMAND INTERPRETER ERROR IS
004100*                    RETURNED IF THE STREAM COMMAND FAILS.
004200*
004300*   STRM-MODE        -  S9(4) COMP - THIS WILL ALLOW FOR FUTURE
004400*                    EXPANSION OF PROGRAM. CURRENTLY IGNORED.
004500*
004600*   STRM CO CODE     -  X(3) - CONTAINS THE COMPANY CODE
004700*
004800*   STRM PRE RUN CARDS - CONSISTS OF UP TO 4 COMMAND CARDS THAT ARE
004900*                        PLACED BEFORE THE RUN COMMAND IN THE JOB.
005000*                        EACH ARE 80 CHARACTER IN LENGTH X(80).
005100*
005200*   STRM RUN COMMAND  - X(80) - CONTAINS THE ACTUAL RUN COMMAND
005300*                       FOR THE PROGRAM TO BE EXECUTED AND
005400*                       INCLUDES A LIB STATEMENT IF NEEDED.
005500*
005600*   STRM JOB NAME    -  X(8) - THE NAME USED FOR THE JOB NAME ON THE
005700*                    JOB CARD.
005800*                    CONVENTIONS.
005900*
006000*   ROUTE CARD       -  X(80) - PASS ROUTE INFORMATION, AS
006100*                    FOLLOWS:
006200*                       NAME OF USER TO ROUTE TO  X(15)
006300*                       USER DEPT                 X(4)
006400*                       PRINTER TO PRINT AT       X(3)
006500*                       USERNAME                  X(8)
006600*                       ACCOUNT                   X(8)
006700*                       GROUP                     X(8)
006800*                       TERMINAL                  X(8)
006900*
007000*   OPTION CARD      -  X(80) - PASS AN 80-BYTE CARD OF OPTIONS.
007100*                    THIS OPTION CARD WILL BE "ACCEPT"ed BY THE
007200*                    REPORT PROGRAM, AND PROVIDE THE REPORT
007300*                    PROGRAM WITH THE OPTIONS SPECIFIED IN THE FRONT-
007400*                    END PROGRAM.  AT THIS TIME, USER OPTIONS THAT
007500*                    EXCEED 80 BYTES CANNOT BE HANDLED BY THIS
007600*                    SUBPROGRAM.
007700
007800*   OPTION CARD2     -  X(80) -  FURTHER REPORT OPTIONS.  PASS
007900*                    SPACES IF NOT USED.
008000*
008100*   OPTION CARD3     -  X(80) -  FURTHER REPORT OPTIONS.  PASS
008200*                    SPACES IF NOT USED.
008300*
      *C
      *C   01MAR1994    DAVE PLUM
